From 0004ca9411992b853af2ac0749191e84b56a1565 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harrison Booth <harrisontbooth@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:10:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Add bounded Windows socket inheritance regression coverage

Regression and test-registration supplement to Bryan Green's original socket inheritance proposal, which must be applied first and retains its original authorship and mail bytes. Production proposal remains Bryan's.

Use the existing recorded local v5 test/helper registration representation. The ordered series remains source-equivalent to the exact hosted combined v5 input; do not apply that combined input as an additional patch.

Force a fresh initdb for this TAP test so it does not rely on the installed initdb template's file attributes when pg_regress configures authentication.

Portable reviewer adaptation and Job-aware joint coverage remain separate.
---
